title: KeeperFirst
---
Keeper: You came through the singing dark. I'm Abri, keeper here. Fold your vanes. The repair cradle's free. #emotion:Tender
Taren: Anything here need looking at? #emotion:Curious
Keeper: Our port docking line keeps going slack. Would you reel it snug once you've rested? #emotion:Neutral
Sela: What's it tied to? #emotion:Curious
Keeper: The old anchorage, out past the port marker. You can reach the reel in flight form. #emotion:Neutral
===
title: KeeperRepeat
---
Keeper: The cradle's yours. When you're ready, have a look at that port docking line. #emotion:Tender
===
title: KeeperPost
---
Keeper: You're patched up, and the beacon's got your log. Rest as long as you like. #emotion:Happy
Keeper: One small job, when you're ready: the port docking line won't stay tight. Would you check the reel? #emotion:Neutral
===
title: SelaTallowLine
---
Taren: Here's the end. Fitting and all. #emotion:Curious
Sela: No anchor? #emotion:Worried
Taren: Nothing on it to pull against. #emotion:Worried
Sela: Look at the marker. It's falling behind us. #emotion:Shocked
Taren: And I don't hear any engines. #emotion:Curious
Sela: The passage is carrying the whole refuge. We're moving with it. #emotion:Intense
===
title: KeeperDriftReturn
---
Keeper: Were you out by the port docking line? #emotion:Curious
Taren: The free end's floating by the reel. Tallow is moving. #emotion:Neutral
Keeper: We're underway? Oh, look at that. The rooms, the cradle, all of it came along. #emotion:Happy
Sela: That's the bend from the nursery, and the turn the Cantor wanted. We'll need a chart that moves with the passage. #emotion:Determined
Taren: Who agreed to go? #emotion:Curious
Keeper: Most of them are still asleep. I never thought we'd actually leave. #emotion:Worried
Sela: Then they should hear it from you. It's their home too. #emotion:Tender
Keeper: Will you stand with me when I tell them? #emotion:Tender
Taren: Yes. Start with the cabins. #emotion:Determined
===

title: KeeperDriftRepeat
---
Keeper: I did the cabins while you were out. Half of them want to turn back, and the rest want a window seat. #emotion:Amused
===

title: CompactHail
---
Keeper: Hold the cabins. There's a voice on the beacon band, and it isn't one of ours. #emotion:Worried
Ilo: Tallow Drift, this is Ilo with the Anchor Compact survey. If you flew the Halo lanes, you passed my cutter. #emotion:Neutral
Ilo: Director Venn runs the Compact's route plan. She's seen your station leave its mooring, and she wants her words read out exactly. #emotion:Neutral
Ilo: "The passages are leaving, and they won't be back in your lifetime. A town that moves will need food, power, and a route that waits for it." #emotion:Neutral
Ilo: "Show me how you'll have all three, and I'll listen." #emotion:Neutral
Sela: She's not wrong about the food. That garden won't feed this place for long. #emotion:Worried
Taren: Then we find some, before she writes Tallow into her footnotes. #emotion:Determined
Ilo: For what it's worth, I hope you manage it. Ilo out. #emotion:Tender
<<setFlag compact.hailHeard>>
===
